{
  "map_info": {
      "name": "The Grid Trace",
      "lookup_name": "Point_Line_Grid",
      "description": "The Grid provides the stable structure of space; the Trace records what happens within it. Where the Line reduces movement to an efficient relation, the Trace accumulates duration—sequence, hesitation, deviation. As a body moves, positions are recorded against the grid, forming a temporary history. Yet this history is bounded: memory is finite, motion is sampled, and deviation is measured relative to fixed frames. The Trace resists reduction, but only from within the grid that enables its capture, leaving a remainder that cannot be fully contained.",
      "description_2": "The Grid formalizes space into a system of addressability. By overlaying a coordinate structure, the map reveals how free space becomes indexed, repeatable, and computable. The player navigates a tension between embodied movement and numerical position, experiencing how grids enable calculation while simultaneously erasing local irregularities. This map exposes the political and technical consequences of choosing a coordinate system.",
